pedersoe@ucsu.Colorado.EDU (Gothmog) writes:

>Does somebody have a list showing the probability of what will occur when you
>step on a magic trap?  I haven't noticed it in a spoiler list anywhere.  Also,
>do the messages "You suddenly yearn for your distant homeland" and "Your pack
>shakes violently" mean anything?  I haven't noticed any changes from either.

You have a 1-in-30 chance of getting caught in a magical explosion
(lose 1d10 HP). The trap is deleted in this case. Otherwise, the
following can happen:

- 50% chance: 1d4 random monsters are generated.

- 15% chance: nothing happens, no message
-  5% chance: nothing happens: "A shiver runs up and down your spine!"
-  5% chance: nothing happens: "You hear distant howling." or "You hear
              the moon howling at you." (when hallucinating)
-  5% chance: nothing happens: "You suddenly yearn for your distant
              homeland." or "You suddenly yearn for Cleveland." (when
              hallucinating)
-  5% chance: nothing happens: "Your pack shakes violently!"
-  5% chance: nothing happens: "You smell charred flesh." or "You smell
              hamburgers." (when hallucinating)
 
-  5% chance: nearby monsters are tamed, no message
-  5% chance: some of your stuff is uncursed (worn objects, loadstones,
              and balls and chains: "You feel like someone is helping
              you." or "You feel in touch with the Universal Oneness."
              (when hallucinating)

